# C-46: MOVC must NOT be recognised as a copy instruction.
#
# On silicon MOVC CONSUMES its source (nulls rs1), and the machine model does not say so:
# hasSideEffects=0, $rs1 a pure USE, no Constraints. The only thing preventing
# MachineCopyPropagation from acting on that unmodelled instruction is that
# CapstoneInstrInfo::isCopyInstrImpl opens with `if (MI.isMoveReg())` and MOVC is not
# isMoveReg. Setting that flag makes MCP treat MOVC as an ordinary register copy, and it will
# then delete "redundant" ones and forward uses across them -- reading a source the hardware
# has already nulled, which is C-32's mechanism.
#
# THIS IS NOT A THEORETICAL PIN. A MachineCopyPropagation instance runs AFTER
# ExpandPostRAPseudos (TargetPassConfig.cpp adds ExpandPostRAPseudos, then addPreEmitPass;
# CapstoneTargetMachine's addPreEmitPass adds createMachineCopyPropagationPass(true), on by
# default), so the pass genuinely holds MOVC instructions. An earlier claim that no such pass
# could ever see a MOVC was wrong, and was retracted after this test was built.
#
# THE MATCHED PAIR IS THE POINT. mv_pair and movc_pair differ only in which instruction forms
# the redundant copy pair. mv_pair is the POSITIVE CONTROL: its ADDI copies ARE recognised
# (isCopyInstrImpl handles ADDI against x0) and MCP deletes them, which proves the pass ran and
# is deleting in this very run. movc_pair must survive. Without the control, a passing test
# cannot tell "MOVC was protected" from "the pass never ran".
#
# DEMONSTRATED 2026-09-10: setting `let isMoveReg = 1` on the MOVC definition and rebuilding
# makes movc_pair lose BOTH movc instructions while mv_pair is unchanged. That is what makes
# the clean run below evidence rather than an unproven gate.
#
# RUN: llc -mtriple=capstone64 -mattr=+m -O2 -start-after=postrapseudos -o - %s | FileCheck %s

# CHECK-LABEL: mv_pair:
# CHECK-NOT: addi
# CHECK: cjalr

# CHECK-LABEL: movc_pair:
# CHECK: movc s0, a0
# CHECK-NEXT: movc a0, s0
# CHECK-NEXT: cjalr

--- |
  target triple = "capstone64"
  define i64 @mv_pair(i64 %a) { ret i64 %a }
  define ptr addrspace(200) @movc_pair(ptr addrspace(200) %a) { ret ptr addrspace(200) %a }
...
---
name:            mv_pair
tracksRegLiveness: true
body:             |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $x10

    $x8 = ADDI $x10, 0
    $x10 = ADDI $x8, 0
    PseudoRET implicit $x10
...
---
name:            movc_pair
tracksRegLiveness: true
body:             |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $c10

    $c8 = MOVC $c10
    $c10 = MOVC $c8
    PseudoRET implicit $c10
...
